{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3223","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3223","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3223\",\"parent_revision\":\"32de8313675d14a3b359559f8e8fa5c14f424ff4\",\"root_revision\":\"268268d64e4ea070571e3b958b62a2930cc7c3de98caab6b0cafeb7b4027e331\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPR #3207 (plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review) added the `review-synthesizer` agent and a new T5 synthesis dispatch stage to the multi-perspective-review skill. `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` was left unchanged, so it still shows the obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\n\\nPer `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, this is a Tier 2 change (new agent dispatched, new Mermaid forks in a SKILL.md) requiring re-extraction of the G4 (concurrency/dispatch topology) and L0/L1 (forks/traces) layers before `assemble_graph.py` can rebuild the graph. Both COVERAGE.md and `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` state that single-pass extraction is prohibited (data must go through the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly pattern) and that the dedicated `dh:workflow-extractor` agent that used to run this is retired, with re-extraction \\\"pending redesign\\\" (see `docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`).\\n\\nBecause the extraction mechanism itself is pending redesign, this could not be done as part of PR #3207 without either hand-editing the layer JSON (explicitly prohibited by COVERAGE.md's \\\"What NOT to do\\\") or running an unvalidated single-pass extraction (explicitly prohibited by workflow-extraction.md's trust boundary rule).\\n\\nUser-provided context: once `dh:workflow-extractor`'s replacement exists (see the PRD), re-run it against `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` to regenerate G4 (and L0/L1 for the new forks), then run `uv run plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` to rebuild `dh-workflow-graph.json`.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:34:09.982085Z</sub>\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` still shows the obsolete four-worker topology with no `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, or Punch List node.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"Grep found zero matches for 'review-synthesizer', 'synthesis-worker', or 'Punch List' in the JSON file.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`; grep -E 'review-synthesizer|synthesis-worker|Punch List' returned no results\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"PR #3207 added the `review-synthesizer` agent and a new T5 synthesis dispatch stage to the multi-perspective-review skill.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"`review-synthesizer.md` agent file exists; multi-perspective-review SKILL.md contains 'T5', 'review-synthesizer', 'synthesis-worker', and 'Punch List' references as dispatch and task naming.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` (exists); `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` contains T5 stage and synthesis-worker agent reference (grep output shows T5 task id, agent reference, Punch List section name)\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"Per `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, this is a Tier 2 change requiring re-extraction of the G4 and L0/L1 layers.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"COVERAGE.md lines 86\u2013101 document the Tier 2 update process: 'Source skill/agent files changed (SKILL.md, reference files, hooks.json)' requires re-extraction of affected layers (L0, L1, G4 per the table). T5 synthesis dispatch is a new agent dispatch, matching the Tier 2 pattern for 'New agent dispatched'.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, lines 86\u2013101 (Tier 2 table)\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n  claim: \\\"The dedicated `dh:workflow-extractor` agent that used to run this is retired, with re-extraction 'pending redesign'.\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"Both COVERAGE.md (line 102) and workflow-extraction.md (line 28) contain the phrase 'pending redesign' with reference to the PRD. workflow-extraction.md explicitly states 'Extraction agents are pending redesign (see the PRD at [../../docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md](../../docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md)).' The PRD itself exists but its Status line (line 3) reads 'Draft v4 amended \u2014 fact-checked 2026-06-16; five design decisions resolved 2026-06-19' \u2014 still in Draft status, not shipped.\\\"\\n  source: \\\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md`, line 102; `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md`, line 28; `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md`, line 3\\\"\\n\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n  claim: \\\"Single-pass extraction is prohibited (data must go through the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly pattern). The ensemble dispatcher scripts (`dh-extract-file.js`, `reduce.py`) exist as the key open question: is the described blocker still real, or has the tooling since been built?\\\"\\n  evidence: \\\"VERIFIED: The prohibition on single-pass extraction is explicitly stated in workflow-extraction.md lines 14\u201322: '3 haiku workers extract independently...`reduce.py --keep-threshold 2` corroborates...A sonnet reducer assembles'. VERIFIED: `reduce.py` exists at `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py`. VERIFIED: Helper scripts `enumerate_scope.py` and `merge_layer.py` exist in `plugins/development-harness/scripts/`. REFUTED: Main dispatcher `dh-extract-file.js` does NOT exist (search