on)\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n\\nNote: APPROVED here means information completeness for planning is satisfied, not that the requested re-extraction can execute today. Every condition resolves to a well-evidenced \\\"not yet possible\\\" \u2014 the item's own Acceptance Criteria must reflect that the actionable deliverable is gated on prd-workflow-extractor.md shipping, not attempt the re-extraction now (COVERAGE.md's \\\"What NOT to do\\\" explicitly prohibits hand-editing the layer JSON or running unvalidated single-pass extraction as a workaround).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:00:40.385597Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: The derived artifact `dh-workflow-graph.json` requires regeneration following PR #3207's source changes (new review-synthesizer agent + T5 stage). The work is not a behavioral defect (system functions correctly) nor a recurring failure pattern. The blocker is the incomplete design of the workflow-extractor tool itself, which is documented as \\\"pending redesign\\\" in `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` and the PRD. The mechanical rebuild task is deferred until the tool design exists to implement it and establish automated gates for future drift prevention.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Decision tree traversal with prerequisite tracing to root cause.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Tool design complete \u2192 automation gate enabled \u2192 artifact regeneration triggered on PR merge\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.231153Z</sub>\\n\\nProducers/targets (will be regenerated or re-extracted): `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/G4-concurrency.json`, `L0-forks.json`, `L1-trace-*.json` (4 files), `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` (embedded data block).\\n\\nExtraction sources (read-only inputs): `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md`, `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md`.\\n\\nRebuild tooling: `plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` (Tier-1 rebuild, already works \u2014 reads layer JSON, no changes needed by this item), `plugins/development-harness/scripts/merge_layer.py`, `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` (both exist, unwired \u2014 part of the pending redesign, not owned by this item).\\n\\nBlocking prerequisite (does not exist, out of this item's scope to build): `dh-extract-file.js` orchestrating dispatcher, referenced by `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` but absent repo-wide.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.231235Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` (lines 86\u2013101) \u2014 Tier 2 update-process definition and the \\\"What NOT to do\\\" prohibition on hand-editing layer JSON.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` (lines 14\u201322, line 28) \u2014 mandates the 3-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration pattern; states extraction agent roles are \\\"pending redesign.\\\"\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` \u2014 PRD for the redesigned extraction ensemble, Status: Draft v4, self-labeled as a historical design snapshot rather than a current spec.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` \u2014 the 23-task SAM plan implementing the PRD.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 full extraction protocol referenced by both COVERAGE.md and the rule file.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` \u2014 the Sonnet verifier agent this item's re-extraction would ultimately dispatch to (currently unreachable, nothing calls it).\\n- PR #3207 (source of the drift) and its review thread (chatgpt-codex-connector) \u2014 origin of this item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.230811Z</sub>\\n\\nScope is narrow and entirely within `plugins/development-harness/docs/` and its producer/consumer scripts \u2014 see the Impact Radius section for the full inventory. Summary: the stale graph affects only human/agent comprehension of the review-dispatch topology via `dh-workflow-explorer.html` and `dh-system-model.html`; no CI, MCP server, or hook reads the JSON programmatically. There is a live but unrelated cross-plugin coupling to note for whoever eventually does the re-extraction: SAM task T07 (upstream `reduce.py` changes, owned jointly with plugin-creator) has been stalled in-progress since 2026-06-20 and sits on the same dependency chain as this item's prerequisite.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:41:14.127874Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` \u2014 the Tier-1 rebuild script (per `COVERAGE.md`). Reads `docs/workflow-layers/{L0-forks,L1-trace-*,G1..G8}.json` and writes `dh-workflow-graph.json` plus the embedded data block in `dh-workflow-explorer.html`. Cannot meaningfully rebuild the T5/review-synthesizer topology until L0 (forks), L1 (traces), and G4 (concurrency/dispatch) are re-extracted from `multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `agents/review-synthesizer.md` \u2014 the assembler only reflects what's already in the layer JSON.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/merge_layer.py` \u2014 merges extraction fragments into a layer JSON file idempotently (owns exactly 3 responsibilities per `plan/architect-dh-workflow-extractor-system.md` \u00a74.2, a plan-storage doc that does not exist as a file in this repo \u2014 architect spec was apparently never persisted). Part of the not-yet-wired redesign; no caller invokes it yet.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/enumerate_scope.py` \u2014 deterministic BFS crawl of the in-scope file set for extraction (ADR-1). Also part of the redesign; exists but is not invoked by anything (its intended caller, `dh-extract-file.js`, does not exist anywhere in the repo).\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-workflow-explorer.html` \u2014 Cytoscape.js viewer that renders `dh-workflow-graph.json`. Will keep showing the stale 4-worker topology with no staleness indicator to the viewer.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_assemble_graph.py`, `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 test the assembler's gap-edge/merge logic itself, not the specific stale data; unaffected by this item unless the assembler's code changes.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/workflow-extractor-reducer.md` \u2014 Sonnet verifier agent for the redesigned ensemble pipeline. References `reduce.py` (exists, owned by plugin-creator), `docs/workflow-layers/extraction-rules.json` (exists), and a `dh-extract-file.js` dispatcher (does NOT exist anywhere in the repo \u2014 confirmed via repo-wide `find`). This agent is currently unreachable: nothing dispatches it.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ensemble-rule-review/scripts/reduce.py` and `plan_ensemble.py` \u2014 owned by the plugin-creator plugin, reused as shared infrastructure by the DH extractor design (confirmed by prior agent-memory, see below). SAM task T07 in `Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` proposes upstream changes to `reduce.py` (slug-normalized heading keys + a `cross_group` signal) gated by a backward-compat protocol \u2014 status `in-progress`, started `2026-06-20`, stalled roughly 2 months as of today (2026-08-29). This is a live cross-plugin coupling: a schema change to `reduce.py`'s output would affect both plugins.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/COVERAGE.md` \u2014 authoritative update-process manifest. Names L0, L1, and G4 as the layers a dispatch/topology change like this one requires re-extracting, and states re-extraction is \\\"pending redesign\\\" pointing at the PRD.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/L0-forks.json`, `L1-trace-*.json` (4 files), `G4-concurrency.json` \u2014 stale source layer data feeding the assembler; none reflect `review-synthesizer` or the T5 stage.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` \u2014 still lists `workflow-extractor-worker`, `workflow-extractor-reducer`, and (implicitly) `workflow-extractor` as canonical agents. Prior agent-memory (dated 2026-06-16, see below) already flagged this as a known-stale inconsistency: the worker and base agent files do not exist under `agents/`, only `workflow-extractor-reducer.md` does.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md` \u2014 full extraction protocol / ensemble pipeline methodology referenced by both `COVERAGE.md` and the `workflow-extraction.md` rule.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/graph-schema.md` \u2014 schema consumed by `assemble_graph.py`; documents the node/edge shapes rendered by the explorer.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/dh-system-model.html` \u2014 links out to the Workflow Explorer; itself classified `generated, not authoritative behavioral contract` in the purpose-audit manifest, and its own Phases 3\u20136 are listed `PENDING` in `COVERAGE.md`'s gap table (pre-existing, unrelated gap).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/meta-workflow-graph-refresh/SKILL.md` \u2014 entry-point skill; points readers at `COVERAGE.md` and `workflow-trace-methodology.md`, inheriting the \\\"pending redesign\\\" blocker rather than stating it directly.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` \u2014 Draft v4 PRD for the redesigned extraction ensemble. Explicitly self-labeled: \\\"Authority: Historical design snapshot. Tool-call forms below are captured extraction patterns, not current executable signatures.\\\"\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` \u2014 the actual 23-task SAM plan implementing the PRD. 22 of 23 tasks are `not-started`; only T07 is `in-progress` (and stalled). Critically, T20 (rewrite `.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` for the new SessionStart/`dh-extract-file.js` design) and T23 (update `dh-workflow-explorer.html` for new node/edge types) are both `not-started` \u2014 the redesign is incomplete even on paper, not just unbuilt.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/audits/purpose-audit-reference-manifest.yaml` \u2014 classifies `dh-workflow-graph.json`, `dh-workflow-explorer.html`, `dh-system-model.html`, `assemble_graph.py`, and `docs/workflow-layers/**` as `generated, not authoritative behavioral contract`. Staleness here does not violate a documented behavioral contract, but confirms these are known-derivative artifacts rather than hand-maintained sources of truth.\\n\\n### Configuration/CI\\n\\n- `biome.json` \u2014 excludes `dh-workflow-graph.json` from formatting (machine-generated).\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 excludes `dh-workflow-graph.json` from a hook pattern, with a comment noting it's machine-generated minified JSON.\\n- No CI workflow validates graph freshness: `grep -rl \\\"dh-workflow-graph\\\\|workflow-extractor\\\\|assemble_graph\\\" .github/workflows/` returns zero hits across all 9 workflow files. Nothing will fail a build or PR check over this staleness.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` (~line 441\u2013444) \u2014 instructs contributors to run `/dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh` after adding skills/agents or changing dispatch logic (exactly PR #3207's change class), but does not itself warn that re-extraction is currently blocked pending the redesign.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md` \u2014 path-scoped rule (`docs/workflow-layers/**`, `docs/workflow-trace-methodology.md`). States extraction \\\"agent roles are pending redesign\\\" pointing at the PRD, and separately flags that the existing L0\u2013G8 layer data (collected 2026-06-08) is itself unverified \u2014 \\\"useful starting hypotheses, not ground truth.\\\" Even a manual re-extraction attempt today would start from data already flagged as suspect.\\n- `.claude/agent-memory/dh-impact-analyst/project_workflow_extractor_cross_plugin_pattern.md` and `.claude/agent-memory/dh-impact-analyst/MEMORY.md` \u2014 prior impact-analyst memory already documents this exact subsystem's fragility: fabricated `workflow-extractor-worker`/`workflow-extractor.md` agents were removed by a prior commit, `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` was already known-stale as of 2026-06-16, and the cross-plugin `reduce.py`/`plan_ensemble.py` dependency was already flagged as a risk. Directly relevant precedent for this item.\\n- `.claude/agent-memory/dh-service-docs-maintainer/dh-mcp-cli-docs.md` \u2014 notes a second, independent gap in the same assembler pipeline: the extraction rule for MCP tool nodes only recognizes `mcp__...(...)` call syntax, not the CLI form (`uv run .../cli.py <command>`) \u2014 relevant if re-extraction work touches the same extraction rules.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- Human developers and AI agents consulting `dh-workflow-explorer.html` or `dh-system-model.html` for the current review-dispatch topology will see 4 workers, not 5 (missing `review-synthesizer`/T5), with no staleness indicator in the UI itself.\\n- No downstream automated system (CI, MCP server, hook) reads `dh-workflow-graph.json` programmatically for gating \u2014 confirmed via the CI grep above. Consumption is human-facing only, via the explorer. So no automated pipeline breaks; only documentation/comprehension accuracy is at risk.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Producers identified (`assemble_graph.py`, `merge_layer.py`, `enumerate_scope.py`)\\n- [x] Consumers identified (`dh-workflow-explorer.html`, `workflow-extractor-reducer.md`, assembler tests)\\n- [x] Cross-plugin dependency identified (plugin-creator's `reduce.py`/`plan_ensemble.py`; stalled upstream task T07)\\n- [x] CI/config checked \u2014 confirmed no gating step exists\\n- [x] Prior agent-memory checked \u2014 matching precedent found and reconciled (this exact subsystem's fragility was already documented 2026-06-16)\\n- [ ] Orchestrating dispatcher (`dh-extract-file.js`) confirmed absent \u2014 re-extraction cannot proceed until this (and its T09/T10-class wiring) is built\\n- [ ] `workflow-extractor-worker` agent confirmed absent despite `KNOWN_ENTITIES.md` still listing it as canonical \u2014 pre-existing known-stale doc, not newly discovered by this item\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.231305Z</sub>\\n\\nBLOCKED on a prerequisite that does not yet exist: this item cannot be executed until the extraction ensemble's orchestrating dispatcher (`dh-extract-file.js`, referenced by `workflow-extractor-reducer.md` but absent repo-wide) is built as part of the in-progress redesign tracked by SAM plan `Pe7547575-dh-workflow-extractor-system.yaml` (23 tasks, 22 not-started, task T07 stalled in-progress since 2026-06-20 with no architect spec ever persisted) and PRD `plugins/development-harness/docs/plans/prd-workflow-extractor.md` (Status: Draft v4). Do not schedule or dispatch this item for execution before that redesign ships the dispatcher \u2014 attempting it earlier would require either hand-editing layer JSON or an unvalidated single-pass extraction, both explicitly prohibited by COVERAGE.md and workflow-extraction.md. No other item or system blocks this one.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.230718Z</sub>\\n\\nP2, unchanged from item creation. Rationale: silent documentation drift only \u2014 the derived graph (`dh-workflow-graph.json`) and its viewer (`dh-workflow-explorer.html`) are human-facing reference artifacts with no automated consumer (confirmed: zero `.github/workflows/*` reference `dh-workflow-graph|workflow-extractor|assemble_graph`). Nothing breaks a build or blocks a PR. Do not raise priority on the basis of \\\"it's blocked\\\" \u2014 blocked-ness reflects a missing prerequisite tool, not urgency of the underlying drift. Re-evaluate priority only if a future item adds CI enforcement of graph freshness, which would convert this from cosmetic drift into a gating failure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.230888Z</sub>\\n\\nOnce actionable, closing this item restores `dh-workflow-graph.json` and `dh-workflow-explorer.html` as accurate references for the multi-perspective-review dispatch topology \u2014 currently anyone consulting them (human or agent) sees 4 workers with no T5/review-synthesizer/Punch List stage, which is silently wrong rather than visibly missing. No functional/runtime benefit (nothing programmatic depends on the graph today), so the benefit is scoped strictly to documentation trustworthiness for future readers of this specific subsystem.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T16:58:43.627451Z</sub>\\n\\n**MISSION_ALIGNED**\\n\\nThe proposed deferral respects the core design constraint for workflow-map maintenance: **no shortcuts on extraction trust boundary**. The development-harness plugin establishes a multi-layered trust boundary (workflow-extraction.md \u00a7Trust boundary, lines 14\u201322) that mandates three-worker ensemble + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly before any layer JSON is committed. This rule exists because single-pass extraction cannot distinguish accurate fields from hallucinated ones.\\n\\nItem #3223 acknowledges this constraint and proposes a deferral-based approach: do NOT hand-edit `dh-workflow-graph.json` (prohibited by COVERAGE.md \u00a7What NOT to do), do NOT run unvalidated single-pass extraction (prohibited by trust boundary rule), but instead WAIT for the designed extraction pipeline (`dh:workflow-extractor` replacement, currently in Draft PRD v4 as of 2026-06-19).\\n\\n**Evidence of alignment:**\\n\\n1. **Respects established rules**: COVERAGE.md \u00a7Tier 2 (lines 86\u2013101) states that agent dispatch changes trigger layer re-extraction and explicitly defers to the pending PRD. workflow-extraction.md \u00a7Agent roles (line 28) states \\\"Extraction agents are pending redesign.\\\" Item #3223 honors both by waiting rather than shortcutting.\\n\\n2. **Rejects prohibited paths**: The PR #3207 review that prompted this item contained a choice: either hand-edit the JSON (prohibited), run a haiku worker pass (prohibited), or defer until tooling exists. The item chooses the rule-compliant path.\\n\\n3. **Aligns with git history**: Six prior PRs address workflow-extraction system design (653635b6a feat, 4333cd244 fix, 9532f99bf feat, 95eb73955 docs, 32519e192 feat) establishing that proper extraction is a prerequisite, not a convenience. No production commit shows layer JSON hand-edits or unvalidated extraction deployments\u2014only ensemble-validated collection (2026-06-08 baseline) followed by the tooling design phase.\\n\\n4. **Architectural consistency**: The extracted layers are the source of truth for `assemble_graph.py` (COVERAGE.md \u00a7Update process, lines 72\u201384). Corrupting that source via hand-edit or unvalidated extraction propagates downstream to every downstream use of `dh-workflow-explorer.html` and any code depending on the graph topology. The plugin chose the higher cost of ensemble validation precisely to prevent this class of bug.\\n\\n**When to activate**: Once `dh:workflow-extractor` replacement ships (PRD tracks this), re-run the ensemble pass over `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md`, re-extract G4/L0/L1, and run `assemble_graph.py`. This backlog item is a standing blocker until that pipeline is available, not a design divergence.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T18:38:51.544385Z</sub>\\n\\nMISSION_ALIGNED \u2014 Item respects the core design constraint for workflow-map maintenance: the trust boundary rule (workflow-extraction.md, lines 14\u201322) mandates 3-worker ensemble + reduce.py corroboration + sonnet-reducer before layer JSON commits. Item correctly defers rather than hand-edit (prohibited by COVERAGE.md \\\"What NOT to do\\\") or run unvalidated single-pass extraction (prohibited by trust boundary rule). COVERAGE.md Tier 2 (lines 86\u2013101) explicitly defers to the pending PRD (currently Draft v4). Six prior PRs (653635b6a, 4333cd244, 9532f99bf, 95eb73955, 32519e192) establish proper extraction is prerequisite. No production commits show hand-edited layer JSON. Architectural consistency: corrupting layer JSON propagates downstream to assemble_graph.py and dh-workflow-explorer.html. Activation: Once dh:workflow-extractor replacement ships, re-run ensemble pass over multi-perspective-review SKILL.md and review-synthesizer.md, re-extract G4/L0/L1, then run assemble_graph.py.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T18:45:19.058172Z</sub>\\n\\n**MISSION_ALIGNED**\\n\\nThe proposed change to defer G4/L0/L1 re-extraction until the extraction tooling exists respects both the trust-boundary rule and the documented \\\"What NOT to do\\\" constraints.\\n\\n**Trust-Boundary Compliance** (workflow-extraction.md:14\u201322)\\nThe existing rule explicitly forbids single-pass haiku worker output: \\\"Unvalidated extraction data is equivalent to a guess.\\\" The proposal defers action until the ensemble pipeline is available (3 workers + reduce.py corroboration + sonnet reducer assembly). This directly honors the established pattern committed in 653635b6a (feat: add workflow-extractor ensemble).\\n\\n**\\\"What NOT to do\\\" Compliance** (COVERAGE.md:109\u2013115)\\n- Line 111: \\\"Do not edit the layer JSON files by hand \u2014 extract from source.\\\" \u2713 Proposal extracts via tooling, not by hand.\\n- Line 112: \\\"Do not edit `dh-workflow-graph.json` directly \u2014 it is an assembler output.\\\" \u2713 Proposal rebuilds via assembler (assemble_graph.py), not direct edit.\\n- Line 113: \\\"Do not restart collection from scratch unless more than 3 layers are affected.\\\" \u2713 Proposal targets G4/L0/L1 (3 layers exactly), staying within protocol bounds.\\n\\nThe proposal also acknowledges that L0\u2013G8 data collected 2026-06-08 was single-pass unverified (COVERAGE.md:37), and defers re-extraction to the redesigned pipeline rather than attempting a shortcut.\\n\\n**Minor note**: The item should specify which plan or PRD gates the re-extraction work (prd-workflow-extractor.md referenced at COVERAGE.md:105), so grooming can link that as a dependency.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.231037Z</sub>\\n\\nThis item cannot be executed today (see Dependencies) \u2014 criteria below describe the externally verifiable end state once the prerequisite ships, not implementation steps:\\n\\n1. Once the ensemble extraction dispatcher exists, re-running the ensemble pipeline (3-worker extraction + `reduce.py` corroboration + sonnet-reducer assembly, per `plugins/development-harness/.claude/rules/workflow-extraction.md`) against `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md` produces updated G4 (`docs/workflow-layers/G4-concurrency.json`) and L0/L1 (`docs/workflow-layers/L0-forks.json`, relevant `L1-trace-*.json`) layer data containing `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, and `Punch List` entries.\\n2. Running `uv run plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` against the updated layer data produces a `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` whose content contains `review-synthesizer`, `synthesis-worker`, and `Punch List` (verifiable via `grep -E 'review-synthesizer|synthesis-worker|Punch List' docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` returning non-zero matches, inverting the Reproducibility check above).\\n3. `dh-workflow-explorer.html`'s embedded data block reflects the same updated topology (5 dispatch stages including T5, not the current 4).\\n4. No hand-edits are made to any `docs/workflow-layers/*.json` or `dh-workflow-graph.json` file directly \u2014 all changes flow through the ensemble pipeline + `assemble_graph.py`, per COVERAGE.md's explicit prohibition.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.230961Z</sub>\\n\\nAfter the prerequisite dispatcher exists and this item is executed: `docs/workflow-layers/G4-concurrency.json` and the relevant `L0-forks.json`/`L1-trace-*.json` files contain entries for the `review-synthesizer` agent, the `synthesis-worker` task, the T5 dispatch stage, and the Punch List artifact/edge, sourced from `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and `plugins/development-harness/agents/review-synthesizer.md`. Running `uv run plugins/development-harness/docs/assemble_graph.py` then regenerates `docs/dh-workflow-graph.json` and the embedded data block in `dh-workflow-explorer.html` to include those same nodes/edges, replacing the current 4-worker topology with the correct 5-stage one (T5 included).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T19:02:21.231376Z</sub>\\n\\nNot estimable as a standalone unit today \u2014 the item is gated entirely on external tooling (see Dependencies) whose own delivery timeline is unknown (PRD still Draft v4, SAM plan largely not-started). Once the dispatcher exists, the re-extraction + rebuild itself is small: re-running the ensemble pipeline against 2 source files (SKILL.md + review-synthesizer.md) for 2 layer classes (G4, L0/L1), then a single `assemble_graph.py` invocation \u2014 comparable in scope to prior single-PR graph updates, likely under an hour of agent/tool time once the prerequisite is available. Do not spend effort estimating this further until the redesign reaches an S5 implementation gate or ships the dispatcher.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\